>> 
>> Perhaps Rodney (and clones) should be generated with a high
>> probability of carrying a wand of banishment, so just as you reach
>> the stairs on level 1 you suddenly find yourself back on level 40.
>> 
>> Another perhaps: it could be a scroll of banishment rather than a
>> wand. That way you get fewer shots, it would banish everything within
>> a certain range, if blessed that doesn't include the reader, if
>> cursed it banishes only the reader, confused: sends the victims to to
>> a dungeon branch that isn't Gehennom, cursed+confused sends you to a
>> random branch of the dungeon (which could be a novel alternative way
>> to find Vlad's tower). 
> 
> It could also send you to Fort Ludios, even if there's no portal in
> that game, and maybe get you to the quest nemesis even if you've
> converted.

I think Fort Ludios would have to be excluded when there is no portal 
otherwise getting back could be problematic. I suppose you could have the 
return portal from Fort Ludious send you into solid rock between dungeon 
levels: an otherwise unreachable place with no stairs, rooms or anything. 
You would then need either level teleport or digging down to get to a real 
level.

> 
> In the endgame elementals can't be banished from their home plane, or
> priests and angel from co-aligned temples, but it would let you get
> rid of the ants - deliberately weak.
> 
I was thinking that as per the original suggestion it would be completely 
inoperative on the planes.


